### MedievalSmalltalk01

medieval-smalltalk01-line1-a = Fair weather today, wouldn't you say?
medieval-smalltalk01-line1-b = Aye, a fine day. May it stay this calm till dusk.

medieval-smalltalk01-line2-a = Have you heard any news from the nearby villages?
medieval-smalltalk01-line2-b = Only rumors, friend. But rumors keep the world turning.

### MedievalSmalltalk02

medieval-smalltalk02-line1-a = Greetings. Roads seem quieter than usual.
medieval-smalltalk02-line1-b = Quiet roads are a blessing. Means fewer troubles wandering about.

medieval-smalltalk02-line2-a = Any advice for a traveler passing through?
medieval-smalltalk02-line2-b = Keep your purse close, your boots dry, and never ignore a warm hearth.

medieval-smalltalk02-line3-a = Sounds like wisdom earned the hard way.
medieval-smalltalk02-line3-b = In these lands, that's the only way wisdom comes.

### MedievalSmalltalk03

medieval-smalltalk03-line1-a = Long road ahead of you, sir knight?
medieval-smalltalk03-line1-b = Aye. The road never ends for those sworn to protect it.

medieval-smalltalk03-line2-a = May fortune follow your steps, then.
medieval-smalltalk03-line2-b = And may your harvest be bountiful in return.

### MedievalSmalltalk04

medieval-smalltalk04-line1-a = Looking for something particular today?
medieval-smalltalk04-line1-b = Just browsing. Sometimes the best finds are unexpected.

medieval-smalltalk04-line2-a = True enough. A keen eye can turn a simple market stroll into treasure.
medieval-smalltalk04-line2-b = Then I shall keep both eyes open.

### MedievalSmalltalk05

medieval-smalltalk05-line1-a = Quiet night, is it not?
medieval-smalltalk05-line1-b = Quiet, yes. But quiet nights tend to hide loud troubles.

medieval-smalltalk05-line2-a = Then may your watch stay peaceful nonetheless.
medieval-smalltalk05-line2-b = And may your travels remain untroubled.

### MedievalSmalltalk06

medieval-smalltalk06-line1-a = You walk with purpose, young one.
medieval-smalltalk06-line1-b = Just trying to make the most of the day.

medieval-smalltalk06-line2-a = A wise habit. Time slips away faster than we think.
medieval-smalltalk06-line2-b = Then I’ll hold tight to what I can.

### MedievalSmalltalk07

medieval-smalltalk07-line1-a = Warm fire and a full mug can mend most woes.
medieval-smalltalk07-line1-b = A welcome thought after a long journey.

medieval-smalltalk07-line2-a = Rest awhile, then. The world outside moves fast enough without us chasing it.
medieval-smalltalk07-line2-b = I just might. This place feels… safe.

medieval-smalltalk07-line3-a = Safety is our trade, friend. That, and a good stew.
medieval-smalltalk07-line3-b = Then you've mastered both crafts well.
